Python Operators
----------------

1. Arithmetic Operators
-----------------------
-Used for calculations
a = 10
b = 5
print(a + b)   # 15
print(a - b)   # 5
print(a * b)   # 50
print(a / b)   # 2.0
print(a % b)   # 0
print(a ** b)  # 100000

2. Relational (Comparison) Operators
------------------------------------
-Used to compare values
a = 10
b = 5
print(a > b)   # True
print(a < b)   # False
print(a == b)  # False
print(a != b)  # True

3. Logical Operators
--------------------
-Used with conditions
a = 10
b = 5
print(a > 5 and b < 10)  # True
print(a > 5 or b > 10)   # True
print(not(a > 5))        # False

4. Assignment Operators
-----------------------
-Used to assign values
a = 5
a += 3   # a = a + 3 → 8
a *= 2   # a = a * 2 → 16

5. Bitwise Operators
--------------------
-Work on binary values
a = 5   # 101
b = 3   # 011
print(a & b)  # 1
print(a | b)  # 7

6. Membership Operators
-----------------------
-Check presence
print('a' in 'akash')     # True
print('z' not in 'akash') # True

7. Identity Operators
---------------------
-Check same memory
a = 10
b = 10
print(a is b)      # True
print(a is not b)  # False



















